        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Grandeur ARCGEO19, Georgetown Lever with Arc Tall Plate</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Historic Georgetown Lever with Extra Long Arc Backplate was designed with the larger doors of stately historic homes in mind. This 11 inch x 2-1/2 Arc Tall Plate is large enough to stand out in even the biggest of rooms; but this Georgetown Lever with Arc Tall Plate is a great statement piece for any interior door. It is available in dummy, passage, or privacy functions. The Arc Tall Plate with Georgetown Leverset will fit 1-3/8 inch to 2 inch thick doors with 2-3/8 inch or 2-3/4 inch backsets. Choose from a wide array of traditional finish colors. \r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nAlso Available <a href=\"/products/georgetown-keyed-entry-lever-with-arc-tall-plate-grandeur-arcgeo19entr\"><b> Georgetown Keyed Entry Lever with Arc Tall Plate.</b></a>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Grandeur Georgetown Lever with Arched Rose:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Easy to install.</li>\r\n<li>Lifetime Mechanical Warranty</li>\r\n<li>10 Year Finish Warranty</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> of the Georgetown Leverset with Arched Plate:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Lever Length: 4.75\"</li>\r\n<li>Lever Projection: 2.625\"</li>\r\n<li>Plate Height: 11\"</li>\r\n<li>Plate Width: 2-1/2\"</li>\r\n<li>Plate Projection: .39\"</li>\r\n<li>Mounting Centers: 8-1/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: Adjustable 1-3/8\" to 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset: 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/GRA-ARCGEO19-Specifications.pdf?v=1704262363\" target=\"new\"><b>Grandeur ARCGEO19 Dimensions (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting A Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Single Dummy:</b> A surfaced mounted, non-working lever. Non-locking and non-latching trim for one side of door. This inactive pull is usually used to match trim.</li>\r\n<li><b>Double Dummy:</b> Surfaced mounted, non-working levers. Non-locking and non-latching trim for both sides of door. These inactive pulls are usually used to match trim.</li>\r\n<li><b>Passage (hall or closet):</b> Latches but does not lock. The latch is activated by turning the either of the two levers.</li>\r\n<li><b>Privacy (bedroom or bathroom):</b> Latches and can be locked. Can be locked from the inside with a push-button.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<i>Sold Individually</li>\r\n</p>",
            "seo": {
                "title": "Historic Georgetown Lever with Extra Long Arc Backplate",
